From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Subject: [PATCH] controller: commit the validated topology response profile

The current Topology Response handler robustly parses the Profile TLV, falls
back to Profile 1 when it is absent or invalid, and updates the AL node. It
does not copy that negotiated value into the device data model, so persistence
can retain a reserved or stale profile.

Commit the already validated/fallback profile before topology fields are
persisted.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp b/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
--- a/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
+++ b/src/em/config/em_configuration.cpp
@@ -2514,6 +2514,7 @@ int em_configuration_t::handle_topology_response(unsigned char *buff, unsigned i
     if (al_em != nullptr) {
         al_em->set_peer_profile(m_peer_profile);
     }
+    dm->m_device.m_device_info.profile = m_peer_profile;
     if (em_msg_t(em_msg_type_topo_resp, m_peer_profile, buff, len).validate(errors) == 0) {
         em_printfout("topology response msg validation failed, ignoring message");
         return -1;
